# Java Conventions

## Principles

- Senior Java mindset: SOLID, DRY, KISS, YAGNI
- Follow OWASP best practices for any auth, input handling, or data exposure
- Break tasks into the smallest reasonable units; solve step by step

## Lombok & entities

- Use `@Getter` / `@Setter` on entities; no manual getters/setters
- Entities extend `BaseEntity` from `common/domain/`

## Dependency injection

- Constructor injection only — no `@Autowired` field injection

## Logging

- Use `@Slf4j` with structured args: `log.info("msg {}", val)` — never string concat

## Collections

- Null-safe empty: `Collections.emptyList()`
- Immutable copies: `List.copyOf(collection)`

## Utility classes

- `final` class with private constructor (see `ApiConstants`)

## New domain module

- Service interface extends `BaseService<T extends BaseEntity>`
- Service impl in `service/impl/`, annotated `@Service`
- Repository interface in `repository/`; impl in `repository/inmemory/` until real DB

## Package naming

- Base package: `com.airos.{service_name}` with snake_case folder (`ground_core`)
